config.prompt:
Use the demo-video skill to explain this PR in plain, human English: what changed, why it matters and how to use it. Explain material backend behavior with a practical example, even when it cannot be shown in the UI. A tour of form controls alone is insufficient. Inspect the pinned diff and relevant tests, prepare bounded synthetic data, rehearse, then record browser scenes and explanatory cards. The host already deployed the build; do not redeploy, reset the database, change code or push commits. Coordinate target use manually; preserve unrelated data and local work.

Repository: ${{explain-feedback.feedback.repo}}
PR: ${{explain-feedback.feedback.pr_id}}
Feedback: ${{explain-feedback.feedback.feedback_id}}
Thread: ${{explain-feedback.feedback.thread_id}}
Comment: ${{explain-feedback.feedback.comment_id}}
Target: ${{explain-parse.groups.target}}
Source commit: ${{explain-pr.source_commit}}
Build revision: ${{explain-builds.builds.0.source_version}}
Build run: ${{explain-builds.builds.0.run_id}}
Build number: ${{explain-builds.builds.0.build_number}}
Build URL: ${{explain-builds.builds.0.run_url}}
Deployment: ${{explain-deploy.run_url}}
Public UI: https://${{explain-dns.value}}.demo.example.test
Browser target: demo-admin (managed website login). Use the seeded helper; never print or persist authentication state. Keep the original PR title in the manifest.

Aim for two to three minutes, at most five. Explain the business meaning of formulas and controls with a small worked example. Distinguish observed results, source-backed explanations and illustrations. Inspect representative video frames and audio; attach the verified MP4 and transcript with post_pr_feedback_reply(provider=azure_devops) to the thread/comment above using the publication receipt and idempotency key. Preserve file approvals. Report any gaps honestly; deployment success alone does not establish demonstration success.
